{"id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch12-noncompact-maximum-principles#cor:l1-heat-uniqueness","title":"cor:l1-heat-uniqueness","path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch12-noncompact-maximum-principles.md","line":236,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch12-noncompact-maximum-principles.tex#cor:l1-heat-uniqueness","uses":["[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch12-noncompact-maximum-principles#lem:absolute-value-harmonic-subsolution]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch12-noncompact-maximum-principles#thm:l1-heat-subsolution-vanishing]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/ch12-noncompact-maximum-principles.tex","label":"cor:l1-heat-uniqueness","line":540,"source":"\\begin{corollary}[$L^1$ uniqueness]\n\\label{cor:l1-heat-uniqueness}\n\\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-ii:page-0183}\n\\uses{lem:absolute-value-harmonic-subsolution, thm:l1-heat-subsolution-vanishing}\n\\dcref{ch12:12.25}\n\\group{Heat Equation Uniqueness}\n\n\nUnder the assumptions of Theorem~\\ref{thm:l1-heat-subsolution-vanishing}, two\n$C^{2,1}$ heat solutions in $L^1(M)$ with equal initial data are equal for all\npositive times.\n\\end{corollary}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\nThe absolute value of their difference is a nonnegative heat subsolution;\napply Theorem~\\ref{thm:l1-heat-subsolution-vanishing}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Corollary</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L^1$\">$L^1$</span> uniqueness] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-636f723a6c312d686561742d756e697175656e657373\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-ii:page-0183</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=reference